# Allowlist, like docker/gems: the context is the repo root, and a denylist
# makes every new large directory a silent context regression.
#
# What stays in: the repo-root files Rails boot reads, the shared cdo config
# and libraries, and the whole dashboard tree including the curriculum.
# The denials under dashboard/ drop dev-machine artifacts that a clean CI
# checkout never has — logs, caches, and the blockly symlink into the apps
# build — so a local build produces the same image CI does.
*
!.ruby-version
!Gemfile
!Gemfile.lock
!deployment.rb
!config.yml.erb
!pyproject.toml
!uv.lock
!.python-version
!python
!config
!lib
!shared
!dashboard
dashboard/tmp
dashboard/log
dashboard/node_modules
dashboard/public/assets
dashboard/public/blockly
!docker
docker/*
!docker/migrate
docker/migrate/*
!docker/migrate/migrate.sh
